WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.935
-Rachel. Oh, I'm so --
-Hi, Jimmy!

00:00:02.935 --> 00:00:04.570
-First of all,
before we even get into this,

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:05.905
I want to thank you
for coming on.

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:07.573
But, also, thank you for --

00:00:07.573 --> 00:00:10.075
for just continuing
to do your job

00:00:10.075 --> 00:00:15.081
and showing up and speaking to
the public because we need you.

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:16.448
And it's important.

00:00:16.448 --> 00:00:19.218
And I know how hard it is
with everything, the pandemic.

00:00:19.218 --> 00:00:22.622
And you just showed up, and it
was awesome what you're doing.

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:24.456
-Well, you know what?
The public needs you, too.

00:00:24.456 --> 00:00:26.058
I mean, we do different things,

00:00:26.058 --> 00:00:29.562
but this thing that we do where
we communicate to lots of people

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:31.631
through the magic television

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:34.367
is a thing that people
want and need,

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:37.370
and we're blessed to be able
to do it through technology

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:40.106
in a way that a lot of people
can't do their jobs safely,

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:41.608
and we can.

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:43.742
And I feel, like,
more privileged than ever

00:00:43.742 --> 00:00:45.845
to have this kind of job.

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:47.146
-You've been covering the DNC

00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:49.415
with Joy Reid
and Nicolle Wallace.

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:51.384
You guys are a great team.

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:53.619
I think we had
some big highlight moments.

00:00:53.619 --> 00:00:56.389
I mean, the first night was --

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:58.290
I think
Michelle Obama's speech

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:00.459
was pretty flawless.

00:01:00.459 --> 00:01:03.629
-Yeah. I mean, she's
Michelle Obama and you're not.

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:06.899
Like, there's nobody like her
in the world.

00:01:06.899 --> 00:01:12.238
She's got this
sort of centered wisdom that --

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:13.739
I feel like she moves people

00:01:13.739 --> 00:01:15.441
in a way
that other people don't.

00:01:15.441 --> 00:01:17.477
And so for her to say,
"Listen, I hate politics,

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:19.345
but I've also seen
the presidency up close,

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:20.980
and if you think
it can't get worse,

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:23.049
I'm here to tell you
that it can."

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:25.318
That, like,
sent a chill through me.

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:27.820
Then her husband speaks
two nights later

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:32.258
and basically warns
that American democracy

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:34.027
could end now.

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:35.328
-Yeah.

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:37.063
-That this could be
the end for us.

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:39.432
And to hear him say that?
He's Mr. Hope and Change.

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:42.468
Like, that was
very unsettling to me.

00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:45.238
-Yeah. Interesting. Yeah.
I got that, too.

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:48.341
I was -- I think it was
more emotional, I think,

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:49.909
just hearing him talk
and be like --

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:53.645
I haven't heard a speech
like this in so long.

00:01:53.645 --> 00:01:54.947
He's so good at this.

00:01:54.947 --> 00:01:57.116
And you go like,
"Oh, this is so --

00:01:57.116 --> 00:02:00.085
I hope everyone out there
sees this.

00:02:00.085 --> 00:02:02.888
I hope every young person
sees this who's going to vote

00:02:02.888 --> 00:02:04.991
or anyone thinking about voting

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:06.526
or what it means
or doesn't mean to them

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:07.927
or 'I'm not going
to vote this year.

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:09.495
I don't know. I don't care.'"

00:02:09.495 --> 00:02:12.465
If you watch this, you go like,
"Wait. What was I thinking?

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:15.301
This is important.
This is our right."

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:19.638
-And he's -- Because he is --
I mean, his brand,

00:02:19.638 --> 00:02:22.608
his whole political message
is about optimism, right?

00:02:22.608 --> 00:02:24.543
It is about what America can be

00:02:24.543 --> 00:02:26.279
and the arc
of the moral universe

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:28.348
bending for justice
and all those things.

00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:30.283
For him to come out
with a warning to say,

00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:32.418
"This is really bad.
We're really at risk.

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:35.622
Our country might not be
a democracy anymore

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:37.423
depending on what happens
in the next election

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:40.026
because the people in the power
now are happy to do away

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:42.061
with democracy
as our form of government."

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:45.297
I mean, hearing that from
some jerk like me, fine.

00:02:45.297 --> 00:02:47.934
Like, that's -- But hearing that
from Barack Obama,

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:51.437
who is not that guy,
it's just --

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:53.205
I just feel like --
Separate and apart

00:02:53.205 --> 00:02:55.007
for how well they're
writing the convention,

00:02:55.007 --> 00:02:56.909
those two speeches
from Michelle and Barack Obama

00:02:56.909 --> 00:02:58.678
are going to stick with me
and I think stick

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:00.946
with a lot of people
for a long time.

00:03:00.946 --> 00:03:03.082
-Yeah, I think
he did a great job.

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:07.954
I thought Kamala Harris equally,
if not better, at holding --

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:11.090
I mean, that was a tough --
You got to follow Barack Obama?

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:13.592
-Barack Obama.
[ Laughs ] Yeah, I know.

00:03:13.592 --> 00:03:15.628
Never, ever, ever, ever, ever.
-It's the number-one rule.

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:17.363
-Never let anybody make you
follow Barack Obama.

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:19.265
-That's the number-one rule.

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:21.033
That's where you just go,
"Yeah, I'm good."

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:22.502
-But, yeah.
I mean, essentially,

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:24.837
he functioned as kind of
the nominating speech

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:27.106
for Kamala Harris.

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:29.308
He referred to her. He didn't
make his speech about her.

00:03:29.308 --> 00:03:31.076
But he referred to her
in the speech as "my friend,"

00:03:31.076 --> 00:03:32.945
and they are actually friends.
They've have actually had

00:03:32.945 --> 00:03:35.581
a really long political alliance
and know each other.

00:03:35.581 --> 00:03:39.218
And I think people who know
that give it some heft.

00:03:39.218 --> 00:03:40.787
But, yeah, I mean,
it's also true

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:42.722
that having a woman of color
on the ticket

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:45.591
for the first time ever
gives you chills.

00:03:45.591 --> 00:03:47.793
And, you know,
for the Democratic Party

00:03:47.793 --> 00:03:50.396
who have had Black women,
women of color, in general,

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:52.398
and Black women in particular,

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:56.703
saving their bacon
for generations now.

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:59.505
Like, no Black women voters,
no Black women doing the work

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:02.775
of the Democratic Party,
no Democratic politicians.

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:05.210
To finally have
an African-American woman

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:07.446
holding that position

00:04:07.446 --> 00:04:09.449
and poised to take that
leadership role in the party,

00:04:09.449 --> 00:04:12.918
it's so overdue,
and it just feels good.

00:04:12.918 --> 00:04:15.421
I mean, seeing her approval
ratings among Democratic voters

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:17.323
is up, you know, north of 90%.

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:19.625
Like, oh, right.
You know, good choice, Joe.

00:04:19.625 --> 00:04:21.928
But then at the end
when she said, you know,

00:04:21.928 --> 00:04:24.630
"In not too many years from now,
people will look back on this,

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:26.765
and they will ask us about
what it meant to be alive

00:04:26.765 --> 00:04:29.468
in this time and they will
not ask us how we felt.

00:04:29.468 --> 00:04:33.439
They will ask us, and we will
tell them, what we did."

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:35.107
I was like -- [ Gasps ]

00:04:35.107 --> 00:04:36.876
I felt like I was, like --

00:04:36.876 --> 00:04:42.315
I feel like future me
is judging current me right now.

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:44.150
And I'm in trouble
because I'm --

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:45.951
Whatever
I'm supposed to be doing,

00:04:45.951 --> 00:04:47.853
I am definitely
not doing enough.

00:04:47.853 --> 00:04:49.355
-Oh.
-And that --

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:52.424
I mean, that's what you want
from a leader, right,

00:04:52.424 --> 00:04:54.727
is to call on
your own moral conscience,

00:04:54.727 --> 00:04:57.496
to call on you
to look inside yourself

00:04:57.496 --> 00:05:00.466
and ask yourself
and ask future self,

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:03.502
ask future you who you want
to have been in this moment.

00:05:03.502 --> 00:05:06.139
-I thought the whole night
was like -- Phew.

00:05:06.139 --> 00:05:07.806
-Yeah.

00:05:07.806 --> 00:05:09.341
-I wanted to talk to you
about, also --

00:05:09.341 --> 00:05:11.343
You had the biggest interview,
I think,

00:05:11.343 --> 00:05:13.178
in the history of MSNBC?

00:05:13.178 --> 00:05:14.847
I may be wrong. £et me know.

00:05:14.847 --> 00:05:17.549
But, I mean, in interviewing --

00:05:17.549 --> 00:05:21.721
Donald Trump's niece,
when she had that giant book,

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:26.058
you got the interview,
and you crushed it.

00:05:26.058 --> 00:05:28.127
When you knew you had
the interview, did you go, like,

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:30.496
"Okay, focus up. What are we
going to talk about?"

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:32.364
Or was it, like,
getting into the mind?

00:05:32.364 --> 00:05:34.233
Like, finally,
"Can I just get in there

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:36.836
and talk to me
about this person"?

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:38.604
-Well, two things about that.

00:05:38.604 --> 00:05:40.873
First of all, I had no idea
that so many people

00:05:40.873 --> 00:05:42.641
were going to watch
that interview.

00:05:42.641 --> 00:05:44.977
Even when I finished
the interview, I was like,

00:05:44.977 --> 00:05:47.013
"Oh, I wonder if we'll get
a little bump from this."

00:05:47.013 --> 00:05:48.347
Like -- [ Laughs ]

00:05:48.347 --> 00:05:49.649
You know sometimes you do a show

00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:51.350
and you're like,
"That was an okay show,"

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:53.219
and then it, like,
turns out to be a blockbuster.

00:05:53.219 --> 00:05:54.620
-Yeah.
-I had no idea.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.789
-Yeah.
-No idea at all.

00:05:56.789 --> 00:05:58.424
But, yeah. I mean,
she has a story to tell,

00:05:58.424 --> 00:06:00.793
and that interview didn't
have anything to do with me.

00:06:00.793 --> 00:06:03.329
It was just that people wanted
to hear what she had to say.

00:06:03.329 --> 00:06:06.298
She's got a really unique
perspective on the President

00:06:06.298 --> 00:06:08.534
and what she thinks
is wrong with him.

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:10.937
-What was the one takeaway,
you think, you can go like,

00:06:10.937 --> 00:06:12.939
"Well, if anyone heard anything,

00:06:12.939 --> 00:06:16.975
you should hear
what she said about this"?

00:06:16.975 --> 00:06:20.212
-I think the thing that
sort of chilled me the most

00:06:20.212 --> 00:06:22.514
and that I've thought about
the most since the interview

00:06:22.514 --> 00:06:24.349
is when she said something

00:06:24.349 --> 00:06:26.819
that actually was very similar
to what Michael Cohen said

00:06:26.819 --> 00:06:28.887
when she did
his Congressional testimony

00:06:28.887 --> 00:06:30.389
before he went to prison,

00:06:30.389 --> 00:06:33.459
which is that she said she has
absolutely no doubt

00:06:33.459 --> 00:06:37.930
that he will not
peacefully agree --

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:41.734
not agree to the
peaceful transfer of power

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:43.536
at the end of his term
if he loses.

00:06:43.536 --> 00:06:44.870
And I don't know if that's true.

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:47.706
He's certainly been stoking
that fear among people,

00:06:47.706 --> 00:06:49.141
but for her to say,

00:06:49.141 --> 00:06:51.210
"Listen. I've known him
since I was a kid.

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:53.045
I've known him
since I was a toddler.

00:06:53.045 --> 00:06:55.748
And I can tell you from
a life's worth of observation

00:06:55.748 --> 00:06:58.484
and every other hard thing
I've ever seen him go through,

00:06:58.484 --> 00:07:01.486
there's no way."
-Whoa.

00:07:01.486 --> 00:07:04.090
-I feel like a lot of
political observers say that,

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:06.091
and we sort of game it out
and think about what options

00:07:06.091 --> 00:07:07.693
will there be then
for the country

00:07:07.693 --> 00:07:09.495
if a president
doesn't want to do this.

00:07:09.495 --> 00:07:12.298
But to hear somebody who, like,
knows him just say that flat-out

00:07:12.298 --> 00:07:16.201
without any equivocation was --
kind of rattled me a little bit.

00:07:16.201 --> 00:07:17.670
-Well, you probably heard

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:19.171
the rumor, too,
that some people say,

00:07:19.171 --> 00:07:21.407
"Well, I think he might
even just quit and say like,

00:07:21.407 --> 00:07:23.709
'Nope. I'm out.
I already got the win.

00:07:23.709 --> 00:07:26.311
I don't want to ever
get a loss on my name.

00:07:26.311 --> 00:07:27.880
-Yes.
-This whole thing's rigged.

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:30.349
And that's it. Bye, guys.
This country's --

00:07:30.349 --> 00:07:32.852
You messed up. And this
whole thing is rigged.'"

00:07:32.852 --> 00:07:34.387
You must have talked about that.

00:07:34.387 --> 00:07:37.156
-I don't know.
I mean, he -- I don't know.

00:07:37.156 --> 00:07:39.291
-Yeah.
-He seems like he's running.

00:07:39.291 --> 00:07:42.561
I don't think that --
If he quit right now,

00:07:42.561 --> 00:07:46.098
he would be elevating
Mike Pence to the office,

00:07:46.098 --> 00:07:48.667
which is something that
I can't really imagine him --

00:07:48.667 --> 00:07:50.068
Like, it doesn't --
It's not like

00:07:50.068 --> 00:07:51.937
it doesn't have consequences.
You know what I mean?

00:07:51.937 --> 00:07:53.839
-Yeah, yeah, yeah. Right.
I didn't think about that.

00:07:53.839 --> 00:07:55.207
-And then if Pence
won the election

00:07:55.207 --> 00:07:56.976
because Trump quit
and gave him --

00:07:56.976 --> 00:07:59.044
I mean, that would be
a mess for him, too.

00:07:59.044 --> 00:08:00.513
I don't know. I don't know.
-Yeah.

